{
  "_readme": [
    "Driver nationalities, the one thing a race result never carries. The pages",
    "each keep an inline copy of the rows they need — they are self-contained,",
    "static, and fetch nothing — and tools/check.py holds those copies to this",
    "file. Add a driver here first, then run:  python3 tools/apply-flags.py",
    "",
    "  countries   ISO 3166-1 alpha-2 code -> the name shown on hover. The flag",
    "              itself is not stored: the pages derive the emoji from the two",
    "              letters, so a code is the only thing that can fall out of step.",
    "  drivers     Driver name, spelled exactly as the page tables spell it, ->",
    "              the country whose racing licence they competed under. That is",
    "              not always where they were born: Mario Andretti raced as an",
    "              American, Alessandro De Tomaso as an Argentine, Dave Charlton",
    "              as a South African.",
    "",
    "Historic states map to their modern successor — Wolfgang von Trips raced for",
    "West Germany, and shows the German flag — because there is no emoji for a",
    "country that no longer has a code."
  ],
